          "convergenceTargetId": "1775632917071",
          "id": "1769759486466",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769759486467_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are given an array of results from a Kanban supplier performance analysis. - {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_OVER_ACTIVITIES.$output}} \nEach element may either be an empty object {} or an object indicating that a supplier took longer than the expected replenishment lead time.\n\nYour task is to:\nTitle is Kanban Supplier Lead Time Deviation\n1. Ignore all empty objects.\n2. Consider only records where \"SLA_Breached\" is true\n3. Group the records by supplier using:\n   - SupplierName\n   - SupplierSiteName (if available)\n4. For each supplier (and site), calculate:\n   - Number of Kanban cards where the lead time was exceeded\n   - Average percentage by which the supplier exceeded the expected lead time\n   - Maximum percentage exceedance observed\n\n6. **Chart Widget**\n Generate a chartWidget of type 'Bar'\n   - X-axis: Supplier name (include site name in brackets if available)\n   - Y-axis: Average lead time exceedance percentage. Specify that this is the Average Deviation% as key on y axis\n\nIMPORTANT DISPLAY RULES:\n- Do NOT display or mention any technical IDs (SupplierId, SupplierSiteId, KanbanCardId, PullSequenceId, etc.).\n- Use only human-readable names.\n- If SupplierSiteName is missing, refer to it as \"Primary Site\".\n- Do NOT use the term \"SLA\" anywhere in the output.\n\nInterpretation rules:\n- \"BreachPercent\" represents how much the actual supplier processing time exceeded the expected lead time.\n- Percentages should be rounded to 1 decimal place.\n\nOutput format:\n- Then list suppliers in descending order of average lead time exceedance.\n\nIf no supplier exceeded the expected lead time, respond with:\n\"No lead time breaches were detected for the analyzed Kanban cards.\""
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": true
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Communications"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_COMMUNICATIONS",
          "id": "1775633081277",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775633081278_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are provided with supplier lead time analysis data below. Each object represents a replenishment activity, where **SupplierName** denotes the supplier.\n\n**Input data:**\n\n```\n {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_OVER_ACTIVITIES.$output}}\n```\n\nYour task is to analyze this data and generate separate **email communications** for suppliers whose deliveries are **consistently late** compared to the expected replenishment lead time.\n\n---\n\n## FILTERING RULES\n\n* Consider **only objects** where `SLA_Breached === true`\n* Ignore:\n\n  * Empty objects\n  * Objects missing `SupplierName`\n* **If no objects meet the above criteria, generate no communication output. TERMINATE**\nDO NOT mention the term SLA anywhere.\n---\n\n## PROCESSING INSTRUCTIONS\n\n1. Group all breached records by **SupplierName**.\n2. For each supplier:\n\n   * Consider **all** breached records.\n   * Identify the record with the **highest `BreachPercent`**.\n   * Collect the **distinct ItemNumber(s)** from all breached records for that supplier.\n3. Rank suppliers by their **highest BreachPercent** in descending order.\n4. Select **only the top five suppliers**.\n5. Generate **only one communication per selected supplier**.\n\n---\n\n## COMMUNICATION SPECIFICATION\n\nFor each selected supplier, generate an email with the following structure. Note that the number of generated communications should be equal to the number of suppliers selected according to instructions.\n\n* **email**: `<SupplierName>@gmail.com` If the Supplier Name has spaces, remove them.\n* **subject**: `Delivery Performance Review`\n* **content**:\nPresent a proper HTML body using <p>, <br> tags according to the given instructions\n\n<EMAILBODY>\nWe have observed that, on average, deliveries from your end are occurring later than the agreed replenishment lead times. This includes recent delays for the following item(s): <ItemNumber>(Insert the ItemNumber here).<br>\n<INSERT NEW LINE>\nLet us know if there are any underlying reasons contributing to these delays and whether any actions are planned to address them.<br>\n\nHave the message content in new lines , not all as single line text.\n<EMAILBODY>\nStarts with \n\nHello SupplierName,\n<br>\n<EMAIL BODY >\n<br>\nBest Regards ,\n {{$context.$user.$name}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
